From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 03:10:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] js: count the cores the system has, not the ones awake at
 start-up

GetCPUCount took sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN). The HP TouchPad parks its
second core while idle (online "0", present "0-1"), so an engine started then
counted one CPU, and with one CPU OffThreadCompilationAvailable is false: Ion
refuses every script over MAX_MAIN_THREAD_SCRIPT_SIZE or
MAX_MAIN_THREAD_LOCALS_AND_ARGS as "too large", and a page of large functions
runs in Baseline only. EaglercraftX 1.8.8's start (TeaVM's large state-machine
functions) took about twenty minutes to reach its texture atlas
(cavekit-eaglercraft.md R6, T-666). The count is now the larger of the online
and the configured cores; the kernel brings the parked core up under load.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MpagfKTnbF5UuSGLUYcN1P
---
 js/src/jsgc.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/js/src/jsgc.cpp b/js/src/jsgc.cpp
index 897273479e..b577a8a288 100644
--- a/js/src/jsgc.cpp
+++ b/js/src/jsgc.cpp
@@ -3072,7 +3072,17 @@ js::GetCPUCount()
         GetSystemInfo(&sysinfo);
         ncpus = unsigned(sysinfo.dwNumberOfProcessors);
 # else
+        // Jihad: the cores the system has, not only those awake at this instant. A device that
+        // parks its second core while idle (the HP TouchPad: /sys/devices/system/cpu/online "0",
+        // present "0-1"; the kernel brings it up under load) gave 1 here when the engine started,
+        // and with one CPU OffThreadCompilationAvailable is false: Ion then refuses every script
+        // over MAX_MAIN_THREAD_SCRIPT_SIZE or MAX_MAIN_THREAD_LOCALS_AND_ARGS ("too large"), and a
+        // page made of large functions (EaglercraftX's TeaVM code) runs in Baseline only
+        // (cavekit-eaglercraft.md R6, T-666).
         long n = sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN);
+        long conf = sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_CONF);
+        if (conf > n)
+            n = conf;
         ncpus = (n > 0) ? unsigned(n) : 1;
 # endif
     }
